    "['forward nexthop [parameter1] out-label [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-lsp-name transit 2.1.1.2 next-hop 2.1.1.2 out-label 20', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress Tunnel10 bidirectional'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress Tunnel10 bidirectional', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the HUAWEI `forward nexthop 2.1.1.2 out-label 20` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-lsp-name transit 2.1.1.2 next-hop 2.1.1.2 out-label 20\\n##\\n\\nThe command configures the forwarding path for a static LSP in Juniper, specifying the next hop address (2.1.1.2) and the outgoing MPLS label (20). This is part of Juniper's static LSP configuration under the protocols mpls hierarchy.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-lsp-name transit 2.1.1.2 next-hop 2.1.1.2 out-label 20'}]]": 1,
    "['backward in-label [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-LSP-name reverse-path in-label 20', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress Tunnel10 bidirectional'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress Tunnel10 bidirectional', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Based on the Huawei configuration `backward in-label 20` (which defines the incoming label for the backward path in a bidirectional static LSP), the equivalent Juniper JUNOS configuration would be:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-LSP-name reverse-path in-label 20\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. The \"bidirectional static-cr-lsp\" concept is implemented using `static-label-switched-path` with `reverse-path` configuration\\n2. The label value (20) remains the same, but the syntax structure follows Juniper\\'s hierarchy\\n3. You would need to replace \"ingress-LSP-name\" with your actual LSP name equivalent to Huawei\\'s \"Tunnel10\" context', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path ingress-LSP-name reverse-path in-label 20'}]]": 1,
