    "['mpls te tunnel-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if the context requires it to be under the interface configuration:\\n##\\nset interfaces Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper typically uses `label-switched-path` for MPLS TE tunnels, and the tunnel-id parameter may be configured either under protocols mpls or directly on the tunnel interface depending on the Junos version and configuration style. The first version is more common for static MPLS TE tunnels in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if the context requires it to be under the interface configuration:\\n##\\nset interfaces Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper typically uses `label-switched-path` for MPLS TE tunnels, and the tunnel-id parameter may be configured either under protocols mpls or directly on the tunnel interface depending on the Junos version and configuration style. The first version is more common for static MPLS TE tunnels in Juniper.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces Tunnel10 tunnel-id 100'}]]": 1,
