    "['ip route-static [destination_ip] [destination_mask] [next_hop]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set routing-options static route 3.3.3.3/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei static route command:\\n\\n##\\nset routing-options static route 3.3.3.3/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2\\n##\\n\\nThis command:\\n1. Creates a static route for destination 3.3.3.3/32\\n2. Sets the next-hop as 2.1.1.2\\nThe Juniper syntax uses \"set\" for configuration and organizes parameters hierarchically under \"routing-options\". The subnet mask is written in CIDR notation (/32) instead of dotted decimal.', 'trans_template': 'set routing-options static route 3.3.3.3/32 next-hop 2.1.1.2'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel-policy [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `tunnel-policy tpatoc` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 transit 2.1.1.2 outgoing-label 20\\n##\\n\\nThis translation:\\n1. Creates an LSP named \"tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2\" pointing to destination 2.2.2.2\\n2. Sets up the static LSP path with the next hop and label information that was specified in the Huawei bidirectional static CR-LSP configuration\\n\\nNote that Juniper handles tunnel policies differently than Huawei, and this translation represents the functional equivalent for establishing the static MPLS TE path.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 transit 2.1.1.2 outgoing-label 20', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 transit 2.1.1.2 outgoing-label 20', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Huawei `tunnel-policy tpatoc` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 transit 2.1.1.2 outgoing-label 20\\n##\\n\\nThis translation:\\n1. Creates an LSP named \"tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2\" pointing to destination 2.2.2.2\\n2. Sets up the static LSP path with the next hop and label information that was specified in the Huawei bidirectional static CR-LSP configuration\\n\\nNote that Juniper handles tunnel policies differently than Huawei, and this translation represents the functional equivalent for establishing the static MPLS TE path.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 transit 2.1.1.2 outgoing-label 20'}]]": 1,
    "['tunnel binding destination [parameter1] te [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the given Huawei configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2\\n##\\n\\nNote: This is the closest equivalent in Juniper for binding a static MPLS TE tunnel to a destination. Juniper handles MPLS TE tunnels differently, and the exact implementation might require additional parameters depending on the specific Junos version and requirements. The above command establishes a static LSP to the destination address.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls static-label-switched-path Tunnel10 to 2.2.2.2'}]]": 1,
    "['mpls-tp meg [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check mip half-function', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI `mpls-tp meg test` command:\\n\\n##\\nset oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check mip half-function\\nset oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check continuity-check transmission interval 1s\\nset oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check continuity-check enable\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) for MPLS-TP OAM functions\\n2. The exact implementation might vary based on Junos version and specific requirements\\n3. The translation assumes basic continuity check functionality similar to Huawei's MEG test configuration\\n4. You may need additional configuration for the full MPLS-TP functionality including MEP settings and thresholds\", 'trans_template': 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check mip half-function'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check continuity-check transmission interval 1s', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the HUAWEI 