e\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. Juniper uses CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) for MPLS-TP OAM functions\\n2. The exact implementation might vary based on Junos version and specific requirements\\n3. The translation assumes basic continuity check functionality similar to Huawei's MEG test configuration\\n4. You may need additional configuration for the full MPLS-TP functionality including MEP settings and thresholds\", 'trans_template': 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check continuity-check enable'}]]": 1,
    "['me l2vc peer-ip [peer_ip] vc-id [vc_id] vc-type [vc_type] mep-id [mep_id] remote-mep-id [remote_mep_id]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep 1 interface ge-1/0/0.1 vlan-id 1 peer 3.3.3.3 vc-id 30000 remote-mep 2', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check mip half-function'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the given HUAWEI MPLS-TP MEP (Maintenance End Point) configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep 1 interface ge-1/0/0.1 vlan-id 1 peer 3.3.3.3 vc-id 30000 remote-mep 2\\n##\\n\\nThis Juniper command:\\n1. Creates an Ethernet CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) MEP at level 1\\n2. Associates it with interface ge-1/0/0.1 (equivalent to GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1)\\n3. Specifies VLAN ID 1 (from the dot1q sub-interface)\\n4. Sets the peer IP (3.3.3.3) and VC-ID (30000)\\n5. Configures the remote MEP ID as 2\\n\\nNote: The exact interface naming might need adjustment based on Juniper's specific interface naming convention for your platform.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep 1 interface ge-1/0/0.1 vlan-id 1 peer 3.3.3.3 vc-id 30000 remote-mep 2'}]]": 1,
    "['cc send [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols mpls-oam meg test continuity-check transmit', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check mip half-function'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the HUAWEI command `cc send enable`, which enables Continuity Check message transmission in MPLS-TP:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols mpls-oam meg test continuity-check transmit\\n##\\n\\nThis command configures the MPLS-TP Maintenance Entity Group (MEG) named \"test\" to send continuity check messages, which is the Juniper equivalent functionality to HUAWEI\\'s `cc send enable`.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols mpls-oam meg test continuity-check transmit'}]]": 1,
    "['cc receive enable', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep ccm-receive enable', 'parent_command': ['set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'set oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain test maintenance-association test-continuity-check mip half-function'], 'root': 'set protocols mpls label-switched-path tpatoc-to-2.2.2.2 to 2.2.2.2', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep ccm-receive enable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei \"cc receive enable\" command enables Continuity Check (CC) message reception for MPLS-TP OAM. In Juniper, the equivalent functionality is configured under CFM (Connectivity Fault Management) which is Juniper\\'s implementation of Ethernet OAM. The command enables reception of Continuity Check Messages (CCM) at the Maintenance End Point (MEP).', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep ccm-receive enable'}]]": 1,
    "['lost-measure dual-ended [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep ccm-loss-measurement dual-ended enable', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep ccm-loss-measurement dual-ended enable', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep ccm-loss-measurement dual-ended enable\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper's equivalent functionality for MPLS-TP loss measurement is configured under OAM Ethernet Connectivity Fault Management (CFM).\\n- The `lost-measure dual-ended enable` command in Huawei enables bidirectional loss measurement, which translates to `dual-ended enable` under CCM (Continuity Check Message) loss measurement in Juniper.\\n- The command is placed in the appropriate context of MEP (Maintenance End Point) configuration in Juniper's CFM implementation.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management mep ccm-loss-measurement dual-ended enable'}]]": 1
